  "meta": {
    "description": "6-max, 100bb cash-game preflop charts. Edit freely: the engine re-parses this file at startup and fails loudly on a typo rather than silently mis-training you.",
    "notation": "PokerStove convention. '77+' = 77..AA. 'AJs+' = AJs,AQs,AKs (high card fixed, low card walks up). 'A5s-A2s' = same high card, low card walks. 'T9s-54s' = same gap, both cards walk down the diagonal. 'AsKh' = one explicit combo. Entries may be a plain string (weight 1.0) or {\"hand\": \"...\", \"weight\": 0.5}.",
    "openerBuckets": "Responses are keyed by how early the opener was: 'early' = UTG or MP, 'middle' = CO, 'late' = BTN, 'sb' = small blind open.",
    "tableSizeMapping": "Charts are 6-max. For other table sizes the last three seats are always BTN/SB/BB, the seat before the button is CO, and remaining early seats split into UTG and MP (extra seat to UTG). Heads-up is BTN vs BB. See seatPositions() in src/engine/ranges.ts.",
    "sources": "Standard solid 100bb 6-max opening and defending ranges. These are the training ground truth for Preflop mode and the starting point for postflop range narrowing."
  },

